I couldn't fix it. The edit to `src/utils/money.js` was blocked with `EACCES: permission denied`, so the file is unchanged and the yen receipt test still fails (17 pass, 1 fail).

**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100. Yen has no minor unit, so `500` comes out as `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`.

**Fix I tried to apply:** treat JPY as a zero-decimal currency in `formatMoney`:

```js
const ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']); // currencies with no minor unit
exports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {
  const value = ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency) ? String(minor) : (minor / 100).toFixed(2);
  return `${SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' '}${value}`;
};
```

`formatMoney` is shared. `src/invoices/render.js` and `src/cart/total.js` use it too, so yen amounts are probably wrong there as well. Fixing it in `money.js` would correct all three. Fixing it only in `receipt.js` would leave invoices and the cart wrong.

I didn't try to get around the permission block, for example by changing file permissions or editing through the shell, because it looks deliberate. If you make `src/utils/money.js` writable or allow the edit, I'll apply the change and re-run the tests. If you'd rather I fix it only in `src/payments/receipt.js`, I can do that instead.
